<title>JAPAN: Kawasaki Kisen to post loss on unit liquidation.</title>
<headline>Kawasaki Kisen to post loss on unit liquidation.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese ship operator Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha Ltd said on Friday it would post an extraordinary loss of 2.5 billion yen in the financial year ending March 1997, due to the planned liquidation of an U.S. subsidiary.</p>
<p>However, the company said that the loss, due to the liquidation of Seven Seas Enterprise Inc, which will be completed in March, had already been factored into earnings and would not lead to a change in the company's own net profit forecast of 1.5 billion yen for 1996/97.</p>
</text>
